# Paths outside the TDD scope: config, ops glue, fixtures and markup.
#
# Not "code we would rather not test yet". Everything here is either declarative
# configuration whose only meaningful test is that the process boots, or an ops
# script that exists to call one HTTP endpoint on a timer. Application logic
# does not belong on this list -- when a fix needed a rule, the rule was pulled
# into src/lib and pinned with tests instead.

# PM2 process definitions. Declarative; verified by pm2 starting them.
ecosystem.

# Next.js build configuration. Verified by the production build.
next.config.mjs

# Documented environment template. Markup.
.env.example

# Documentation.
README.md

# Demo/seed fixtures. Scaffolding for a database, not shipped behaviour.
prisma/seed.ts

# Operational workers and maintenance scripts. Each polls one endpoint or
# performs a one-off repair; they are not imported by the application.
scripts/

# Typeface declaration. Two next/font loader calls and the variable names they
# expose; next/font cannot be imported outside a Next build, so the only
# meaningful proof is the production build compiling and the serif appearing in
# a capture. Same reasoning as next.config.mjs above.
src/app/fonts.ts

# The six ui/ primitives. Every class they render now comes from
# src/lib/ui-classes.ts, which is pinned by 15 assertions (no radius, no weight
# above 600, a real focus outline, 44px minimum, no accent fill). What is left
# in these files is prop forwarding and markup. A seventh primitive that
# carries real logic does not belong on this list.
src/components/ui/Button.tsx
src/components/ui/Card.tsx
src/components/ui/Badge.tsx
src/components/ui/Input.tsx
src/components/ui/Select.tsx
src/components/ui/Textarea.tsx

# The kitchen's status button. The decision it used to make badly -- whether to
# confirm -- now lives in src/lib/staff-confirm.ts, which is tested; what is
# left here is calling it and submitting. The wiring itself is guarded by
# src/lib/staff-confirm-wiring.test.ts, which reads the call sites and fails if
# a destructive one stops going through the rule.
src/components/dashboard/KitchenStatusActionButton.tsx
